      "text": "Let's break down the problem step-by-step to find the total area of the logo and then determine the shaded area. The logo consists of four smaller circles inside a square with a side length of 8 inches. The area of the square is \\(8^2 = 64\\) square inches. \n\nThe radius of each smaller circle is \\(4/2 = 2\\) inches.\n\nSo the area of one circle is \\(\\pi (radius)^2 = \\pi (2)^2 = 4\\pi\\) square inches.\n\nTherefore, the total shaded area is the area of the square minus the area of the four circles:\n\n\\[64 - 4 \\times 4\\pi = 64 - 16\\pi\\]\n\nWe will now calculate this using Python for accuracy.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# side length of the square\nside_length = 8\n\n# radius of each circle\nradius = side_length / 4\n\n# area of the square\nsquare_area = side_length ** 2\n\n# area of one circle\ncircle_area = math.pi * radius ** 2\n\n# total shaded area\nshaded_area = square_area - 4 * circle_area\n\nprint(shaded_area)\n```\n```output\n12.918136287871412\n```\nThe total shaded area of the logo, which is \\(\\boxed{64 - 16\\pi}\\) square inches, evaluates to approximately \\(12.92\\) square inches.",
